   "text": {
    "L1": "A factor divides a number exactly, with nothing left over.",
    "L2": "To find every factor of 28, test numbers in order and make multiplication pairs.",
    "L3": "Start with 1: one times 28 equals 28. Then 2 times 14 equals 28.",
    "L4": "Three does not divide 28, but 4 times 7 does.",
    "L5": "The factors are 1, 2, 4, 7, 14 and 28. One and the number itself are included.",
    "L6": "After 6 times 6, factor pairs repeat the other way round, so stop looking.",
    "L7": "Do not list factors at random. Pairing helps you find every one without missing any."
   },
